# What the recipe hash covers: every committed file under these paths, at HEAD. A change to any of
# them makes a different image, so the hash changes, and a robot built from that commit refuses to
# deploy against coprocessors flashed from an older one until they're reflashed.
#
# The definition, for any other implementation (the robot build computes the same value):
#   recipe hash = sha256 of the output of
#     git ls-tree -r --full-tree HEAD -- <each path below, in this order>
#   as lowercase hex. Lines here that are blank or start with # are ignored.
#
# Documentation and tests are left out on purpose: changing them changes no image. The build files
# that build the agent's jar are in: a change to them changes the recipe, and the coprocessors need
# a new release. The version catalog (gradle/libs.versions.toml) is left out on purpose, so the
# weekly dependency updates don't each demand one: an updated library (the agent's SQLite driver)
# reaches the boards with the next image built for another reason.
# test/recipe_test.sh checks that everything provision.sh reads from the repository is covered.
coprocessor/image/provision.sh
coprocessor/image/layout.sh
coprocessor/image/stamp.sh
coprocessor/image/stamp-image.sh
coprocessor/image/lib
coprocessor/image/boards
coprocessor/image/files
coprocessor/photonvision.lock
coprocessor/agent/coprocessor-agent.service
coprocessor/agent/src/main
coprocessor/agent/build.gradle
coprocessor/common/src/main
coprocessor/common/build.gradle
build.gradle
settings.gradle
gradle/quality.gradle
gradle/gradle-daemon-jvm.properties
gradle/wrapper
